Package: libpolycall1
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Polycall polyglot interoperability core (shared library)
 Polycall is a small C core that language bindings load over a stable C
 ABI (Binding ABI v1: plain scalars, UTF-8 strings, caller-owned buffers,
 validated handles). It provides configuration parsing, a deadline-bounded
 RPC runtime and an authenticated peer-to-peer message transport.
 .
 This package contains the shared library libpolycall.so.1.

Package: libpolycall-dev
Section: libdevel
Architecture: any
Multi-Arch: same
Depends: libpolycall1 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Polycall polyglot interoperability core (development files)
 Polycall is a small C core that language bindings load over a stable C
 ABI.
 .
 This package contains the headers (include/polycall), the static library,
 the pkg-config file (polycall.pc) and the CMake package
 (find_package(polycall) -> polycall::polycall).

Package: polycall
Section: net
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Polycall command line interface and daemon
 The polycall executable: configuration checks, RPC calls, the peer
 transport, and `polycall daemon` with a hardened systemd unit
 (polycall.service, DynamicUser, Type=notify).
 .
 The unit is installed but neither enabled nor started; configure
 /etc/polycall/Polycallfile and run `systemctl enable --now polycall`.
